  "description": "Avalonia LinuxFramebuffer/DRM support for the ifm CR1140/CR1141/CR1102 ecomatDisplay panels — CR1140/CR1141: 4.3\" 800×480 keypad-only (NXP i.MX 8M Nano / aarch64); CR1102: 10\" 1280×800 PCAP touchscreen + keypad (quad-core ARM 1.2 GHz + GPU). Custom IInputBackend (EvdevKeypadInput) reads the gpio-keys keypad from /dev/input/event1 (evdev) — Avalonia's built-in LinuxFramebuffer input handles touch/pointer only, so keypad-only SKUs need this. Two software (Skia) output backends with display rotation for mounting the panel in any orientation: RotatingFbdevOutput (single-buffered /dev/fb0) and RotatingDrmOutput (tear-free DRM/KMS DUMB double-buffer + page-flip on /dev/dri/card0). Resolution-agnostic: reads the panel mode at runtime, supports 800×480 and 1280×800. SoftKeyFooter control with physical-keypad or natural (F1..F6) ordering, status-LED and keypad-backlight control with animation modes (LedSysfs/LedMode/LedDriver over /sys/class/leds), …",
