  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "0.15.0 — Multi-targets net8.0, net9.0 and net10.0 (previously net8.0 only): the package now ships lib/net8.0, lib/net9.0 and lib/net10.0 assemblies, so consumers on any of the three runtimes resolve a matching build instead of running the net8.0 assembly on a roll-forward. Adds a device-agnostic keypad button backlight — the new Cr1140.Avalonia.Leds.KeypadBacklight picks the right transport per SKU behind one KeypadBacklight.For(profile) entry point: the sysfs *:kbd_backlight PWM LED (CR1140/CR1141, animated LedMode curves) or the com.ifm.Keyboard keyboard-MCU D-Bus keys (CR1102, solid); every operation is fail-soft off-device. The rest of the public API — input backends, SoftKeyFooter, LED/backlight control, telemetry, perf overlay, device profiles and desktop emulator — is unchanged from 0.14.0. Still requires Avalonia 12 (12.1.3); consumers must reference Avalonia 12.x (Avalonia 11 is not supported).",
